course: dictionary
lesson: 13123
title: Fluency
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fluency means doing something smoothly, easily and well, without stopping to struggle. A fluent reader reads at a good speed, with expression, and does not have to sound out every word. «Maya read the story with fluency, and her friends clapped.»
explain: Fluency can also be about a language. «Sam has fluency in French after living in Paris for a year.» This means he can speak French easily and well. Fluency does not come straight away. You gain it through practice, a little every day.
explain: In maths, fluency means knowing number facts and methods quickly and accurately. «Ravi's fluency with times tables helped him finish the test early.» He did not have to work out 7 times 8 each time, because he just knew it.
fact: Fluency means doing something smoothly, easily and well.
fact: «Reading fluency» means reading at a good speed, with expression.
fact: «Fluency in French» means speaking or reading French easily.
fact: You gain fluency through practice, not by being told about it once.
fact: In maths, fluency means knowing number facts quickly and accurately.
exercise: «Maya read the story with fluency.» What does fluency mean here? | Not reading at all | *Reading smoothly and easily, with expression | Reading very slowly, one letter at a time | Shouting the words loudly
exercise: «Sam has fluency in French.» What does this tell you about Sam? | He is learning to draw in French | He has forgotten all his French | *He can speak French easily and well | He has never heard French
exercise: Ravi says fluency with times tables means counting on his fingers each time. What does fluency really mean in maths? | Guessing the answer quickly | Counting slowly and carefully | *Knowing number facts quickly and accurately | Writing the sums in a neat row
test: «Lena reads with fluency, so she does not stop at every word.» What does fluency mean? | *Reading smoothly and easily | Reading backwards | Reading only in her head | Reading in a whisper
test: Which phrase names a language you can speak easily? | Mandarin homework | *Fluency in Mandarin | a Mandarin lesson on Monday | a Mandarin dictionary
exam: Mia says, «Practice helps you gain fluency in a new language.» What does gain fluency mean? | Stop practising | *Get better at speaking easily | Forget your first language | Lose all your words
